text: ['Activated abilities of nontoken Rebels cost an additional "Sacrifice a land" to activate.', 'All combat damage that would be dealt to you this turn by target unblocked creature is dealt to its controller instead.', 'As Heightened Awareness enters the battlefield, discard your hand.\\nAt the beginning of your draw step, draw an additional card.', "At the beginning of each player's end step, Citadel of Pain deals X damage to that player, where X is the number of untapped lands they control.", "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player mills a card. Then they create X 1/1 black Minion creature tokens, where X is the milled card's mana value.", 'At the beginning of your end step, if you control no untapped lands, draw a card.', 'At the beginning of your end step, if you control no untapped lands, you gain 2 life.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Darba unless you pay {G}{G}.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Whipstitched Zombie unless you pay {B}.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may exile a land card from your graveyard. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', "Basic lands each player controls have shroud as long as that player controls three or fewer lands. (They can't be the targets of spells or abilities.)", "Branded Brawlers can't attack if defending player controls an untapped land.\\nBranded Brawlers can't block if you control an untapped land.", 'Celestial Convergence enters the battlefield with seven omen counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove an omen counter from Celestial Convergence. If there are no omen counters on Celestial Convergence, the player with the highest life total wins the game. If two or more players are tied for highest life total, the game is a draw.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {X}, where X is its mana value.', 'Creatures you control get +0/+1 until end of turn. They get an additional +0/+2 until end of turn unless any player pays {2}.', 'Creatures you control get +7/+7 until end of turn.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{3}: Destroy Wall of Vipers and target creature it's blocking. Any player may activate this ability.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{4}: Return Quicksilver Wall to its owner's hand. Any player may activate this ability.", "Destroy all creatures you don't control. They can't be regenerated.", "Destroy all enchantments you don't control. Then if you control an untapped land, destroy all enchantments you control.", 'Destroy target land. Devastate deals 1 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Destroy target land. Its controller loses 2 life.', 'Draw three cards. Then if any player pays {2}, discard three cards.', 'Each player creates a green Elephant creature token. Those creatures have "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in its controller\'s graveyard."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can block any number of creatures.', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}."', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn."', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn."', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: This land deals 1 damage to any target."', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: This land deals 1 damage to each creature and each player."', "Enchant land\\nEnchanted land is a 5/6 green Treefolk creature that's still a land.", 'Exile target attacking creature unless its controller pays {X}.', "Fen Stalker has fear as long as you control no untapped lands. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'First strike\\n{2}: Zerapa Minotaur loses first strike until end of turn. Any player may activate this ability.', 'Flash\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+2.', 'Flash\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -3/-0.', "Flash\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Flash\\nEnchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals combat damage to defending player, you may destroy target artifact that player controls.', 'Flash\\nEnchant creature\\n{1}{G}: Regenerate enchanted creature.', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nSacrifice Spiketail Hatchling: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.", 'Flying, first strike\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Pit Raptor unless you pay {2}{B}{B}.', 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your end step, tap all lands you control.', 'Flying\\nSacrifice Spiketail Drake: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.', "Flying\\nSacrifice a land: Return Stormwatch Eagle to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nSacrifice two lands: Jeweled Spirit gains protection from artifacts or from the color of your choice until end of turn.', "Flying\\nWhen Windscouter attacks or blocks, return it to its owner's hand at end of combat. (Return it only if it's on the battlefield.)", 'Flying\\n{2}: Ribbon Snake loses flying until end of turn. Any player may activate this ability.', 'Flying\\n{T}, Sacrifice X lands: Put X +1/+1 counters on Copper-Leaf Angel.', 'Flying\\n{T}, Sacrifice a land: Search your library for a Mercenary permanent card with mana value 2 or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "Hazy Homunculus can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an untapped land.", "Hollow Warrior can't attack or block unless you tap an untapped creature you control not declared as an attacking or blocking creature this combat. (This cost is paid as attackers or blockers are declared.)", "If an opponent controls at least four more creatures than you, this spell costs {6} less to cast.\\nTrample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'If an opponent controls seven or more lands, this spell costs {6} less to cast.\\nFlying\\n{R}: Avatar of Fury gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'If an opponent has no cards in hand, this spell costs {6} less to cast.\\nFlying', "If there are ten or more creature cards total in all graveyards, this spell costs {6} less to cast.\\nFear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\n{T}: Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'If you have 3 or less life, this spell costs {6} less to cast.\\nFlying\\nAvatar of Hope can block any number of creatures.', 'Inflame deals 2 damage to each creature dealt damage this turn.', "Lands target player controls don't untap during their next untap step.", "Mercenaries don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", "Mercenary Informer can't be the target of black spells or abilities from black sources.\\n{2}{W}: Put target nontoken Mercenary on the bottom of its owner's library.", 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt to Glittering Lion.\\n{3}: Until end of turn, Glittering Lion loses "Prevent all damage that would be dealt to Glittering Lion." Any player may activate this ability.', 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt to Glittering Lynx.\\n{2}: Until end of turn, Glittering Lynx loses "Prevent all damage that would be dealt to Glittering Lynx." Any player may activate this ability.', 'Protection from white\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Bog Elemental unless you sacrifice a land.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on each of X target creatures.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nSacrifice a land: Spitting Spider deals 1 damage to each creature with flying.', "Rebel Informer can't be the target of white spells or abilities from white sources.\\n{3}: Put target nontoken Rebel on the bottom of its owner's library.", "Reorder your graveyard at random. An opponent chooses a card at random in your graveyard. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, exile it.", "Return target creature to its owner's hand. Then return another target creature to its owner's hand unless its controller pays {1}.", 'Return two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand unless any player pays {X}.', "Rhystic Lightning deals 4 damage to any target unless that permanent's controller or that player pays {2}. If they do, Rhystic Lightning deals 2 damage to the permanent or player.", 'Sacrifice Spore Frog: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Sacrifice a land: Coastal Hornclaw gains flying until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice a land: Destroy target enchantment.', 'Sacrifice a land: Fault Riders gets +2/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', 'Sacrifice a land: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', 'Sacrifice a land: Trenching Steed gets +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice two lands: Return Coffin Puppets from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep and only if you control a Swamp.', 'Scoria Cat gets +3/+3 as long as you control no untapped lands.', "Search target player's library for up to seven cards and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", 'Searing Wind deals 10 damage to any target.', 'Spur Grappler gets +2/+1 as long as you control no untapped lands.', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", 'Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn. Another target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn. That creature gets an additional +4/+4 until end of turn unless any player pays {2}.', 'Target player discards a card at random. Then that player discards another card at random unless they pay {1}.', "Target player reveals their hand. You choose an instant or sorcery card from it and exile that card. You may cast that card for as long as it remains exiled. At the beginning of the next end step, if you haven't cast the card, return it to its owner's hand.", "Target player's life total becomes 20.", 'Trample', "Trample\\nKeldon Battlewagon can't block.\\nWhen Keldon Battlewagon attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.\\nTap an untapped creature you control: Keldon Battlewagon gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the power of the creature tapped this way.", 'Trample\\n{3}: Vintara Elephant loses trample until end of turn. Any player may activate this ability.', 'Unless any player pays {2}, search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Unless target player pays {3}, that player loses 5 life and you gain 5 life.', "Up to three target creatures can't block this turn.", "Veteran Brawlers can't attack if defending player controls an untapped land.\\nVeteran Brawlers can't block if you control an untapped land.", "Vintara Snapper has shroud as long as you control no untapped lands. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'When Gulf Squid enters the battlefield, tap all lands target player controls.', 'When Keldon Firebombers enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices all lands they control except for three.', 'When Silt Crawler enters the battlefield, tap all lands you control.', 'When there are no creatures on the battlefield, sacrifice Task Mage Assembly.\\n{2}: Task Mage Assembly deals 1 damage to target creature. Any player may activate this ability but only as a sorcery.', "Whenever Death Charmer deals combat damage to a creature, that creature's controller loses 2 life unless they pay {2}.", 'Whenever Fickle Efreet attacks or blocks, flip a coin at end of combat. If you lose the flip, an opponent gains control of Fickle Efreet.', 'Whenever Keldon Berserker attacks, if you control no untapped lands, it gets +3/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Lesser Gargadon attacks or blocks, sacrifice a land.', 'Whenever Plague Fiend deals combat damage to a creature, destroy that creature unless its controller pays {2}.', "Whenever Shrouded Serpent attacks, defending player may pay {4}. If that player doesn't, Shrouded Serpent can't be blocked this turn.", "Whenever Soul Charmer deals combat damage to a creature, you gain 2 life unless that creature's controller pays {2}.", 'Whenever Thresher Beast becomes blocked, defending player sacrifices a land.', "Whenever a nontoken creature enters the battlefield, its controller creates a token that's a copy of that creature.\\nWhenever a nontoken creature leaves the battlefield, exile all tokens with the same name as that creature.\\nWhen Dual Nature leaves the battlefield, exile all tokens created with Dual Nature.", "Whenever a player puts a nontoken creature onto the battlefield, that player returns a land they control to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, you may draw a card unless that player pays {1}.', 'Whenever one or more creatures attack you, if Reveille Squad is untapped, you may untap all creatures you control.', 'Wing Storm deals damage to each player equal to twice the number of creatures with flying that player controls.', 'Wintermoon Mesa enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Wintermoon Mesa: Tap two target lands.', "You can't untap more than one land during your untap step.", "You may discard a Forest card rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nPrevent all combat damage that would be dealt by unblocked creatures this turn.", "You may discard a Mountain card rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nFlameshot deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three target creatures.", "You may discard a Plains card rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nDestroy target artifact or enchantment.", "You may discard a Swamp card rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nChoose a creature type. All creatures of that type get -1/-1 until end of turn.", "You may discard an Island card and another card rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nCounter target spell.", '{0}: Tap all lands you control. Chimeric Idol becomes a 3/3 Turtle artifact creature until end of turn.', '{1}, Sacrifice a land: Draw a card. Any player may activate this ability.', '{1}, Sacrifice two lands: Destroy target land.', '{1}: Any player may pay {1}. If no one does, the next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}{B}, Sacrifice a land: Target creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice a land: Create two 1/1 green Squirrel creature tokens.\\n{1}{G}, Sacrifice a land: Squirrel creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{2}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn. Any player may activate this ability.', "{2}{G}, {T}, Discard two cards: All lands target player controls become 3/3 creatures until end of turn. They're still lands.", '{2}{W}: The next time target attacking creature would deal combat damage to Shield Dancer this turn, that creature deals that damage to itself instead.', "{2}{W}{W}, {T}, Discard two cards: Destroy all creatures except for Mageta the Lion. Those creatures can't be regenerated.", "{4}: Return target creature card from a graveyard to its owner's hand. Any player may activate this ability but only as a sorcery.", '{B}: Nakaya Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn unless any player pays {2}.', '{B}: Regenerate Chilling Apparition.\\nWhenever Chilling Apparition deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card.', '{R}: Ridgeline Rager gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{R}: Target creature gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack this turn.)', '{T}, Sacrifice Mine Bearer: Destroy target attacking creature.', '{T}: Choose a color. Add one mana of that color unless any player pays {1}. Activate only as an instant.', '{U}: Tap target creature unless its controller pays {1}.', '{W}{W}: Target attacking creature gets -1/-0 until end of turn.', '{X}{B}, {T}, Discard two cards: Target player discards X cards at random.', '{X}{R}, {T}, Discard two cards: Latulla, Keldon Overseer deals X damage to any target.', "{X}{U}, {T}, Discard two cards: Return X target creatures to their owners' hands."]
flavor: ['"All mages dip into the same well; some are just in more of a hurry."\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"Are you *sure* you want to do that?"', '"Battle is our religion. This fortress is our temple."\\n—Latulla, Keldon overseer', '"Creation is no great feat. Anything you make, I can unmake in a heartbeat."\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"Doesn\'t look like much, does it?"\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"Enemies can be your weapons or your shields. Simply show them which they are."\\n—*The Teachings of Zho*', '"Everything around her suffers."\\n—Haddad, Kipamu soldier', '"Fields can be replanted. Settlements can be rebuilt. Burn it all."\\n—Latulla, Keldon overseer', '"Gnawed to death. Bad way to go."', '"Go ahead. Take it. You\'ll be so very powerful . . . and what harm can it do?"', '"I need no army. I have Jamuraa."', '"I\'ll rain down on you with the power of magic itself. Then we\'ll see who prevails."\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"If there isn\'t enough of Jamuraa left to stand on, I will still claim it for Keld."\\n—Latulla, Keldon overseer', '"It matters not if the gods hear my prayers. Jamuraa does."', '"It startles me how alive one feels on the edge of death."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Ogg hit wall. Ogg no kill wall. Ogg hate wall!"', '"Tell me again," said Latulla, raising her fist, "how just one woman held back an entire Keldon platoon."', '"The Keldons may have explosive tempers, but *I* have explosives."', '"The fifth wind of ascension is Exalter, fulfilling Keld\'s destiny."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The first wind of ascension is Forger, burning away impurity."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The fourth wind of ascension is Anointer, deifying the worthy."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The second wind of ascension is Reaver, slaying the unworthy."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The snapper is still when all else moves\\nAnd strikes when all are dozing."\\n—*Tales of the Vintara Forest*', '"The spell will have to wait," said Alexi, pointing up. "Drakes."', '"The sword or the lash. Choose."\\n—Akul, Keldon whip sergeant', '"The third wind of ascension is Eliminator, clearing Keld\'s path to victory."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The trick is to ask when no one\'s listening."\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"There are secrets out there begging to be rediscovered. We just need to look in the right places."\\n—Teferi, planeswalker', '"They no longer care about their own suffering. Show them something worse."\\n—Latulla, Keldon overseer', '"To arms! To arms! The Lion roars!"', '"War destroys; nature renews."\\n—Jolrael, empress of beasts', '"We outnumber them! Charge! Charge! Hey, where\'d you guys go? Retreat! Retreat!"', '"We wait and watch, and as we prepare for war, we grow strong."', '"When Serra made angels, people called her a goddess. My angels are far superior to hers."\\n—Latulla, Keldon overseer', '"When the bog walks, the wise run."\\n—Erissa, bog witch', '"Which is worse: nothing to defend, or no one to defend it?"', '"You\'re Latulla\'s gift to me, and I always play with my presents."', '"You\'re willing to die for your homeland. I\'m willing to kill for it."\\n—Latulla, Keldon overseer', 'A shield for one is good. A shield for everyone is even better.', 'A thousand wings beating as one can choke the sky itself.', 'After a chimeric idol attacked them, the Keldons smashed all unfamiliar statues.', 'All snakes slither. Only this one soars.', 'Any lock can be undone, any secret revealed.', 'As a rite of passage, Kipamu youths taunt razorbacks with long sticks . . . then flee.', 'As erratic and turbulent as a summer squall.', 'As he knows all the world completely, the world refuses him harm.', 'As silent as a shadow, and just as hard to flee.', 'As the strange plague ravaged Jamuraa, the fiends multiplied.', 'As war raged on, the young mages became more direct in their tactics, often at great cost.', 'Cities have crumbled under its weight.', 'Dark is light and day is night When the winter moon shines.', 'Death awaits them on both fronts.', "Everyone is manipulated. It's just more obvious with the dead.", "Everything it sees it considers food—and with that many eyes, it's not liable to miss much.", 'First death. Then Shauku.', 'Flame chooses its own course.', 'Friends teach what you want to know. Enemies teach what you *need* to know.', 'Grapplers hunt in packs, driving their victims over steep mountain cliffs.', "Greel's grin is far less loathsome than his touch.", 'If it could capture the power it wastes, it would be invincible.', 'If they could replenish the land instead of draining it, Jamuraa would be teeming with them.', 'In the jungle of war there is always a Lion.', 'It destroys everything in its path, including the path itself.', 'It dodges waves of water to prepare for waves of magic.', 'It vents the chill of the grave.', "Jamuraa's rhystic mages treat magic as their garden, uprooting unwanted spells as bothersome weeds.", 'Jamuraan farmers fear three things above all else: droughts, floods, and hornclaws.', 'Jamuraan wizards are linked together by magic, a bond that only the wicked dare exploit.', 'Jolrael tends the land so that the land will tend the beasts.', 'Keldon soldiers learn to move faster than the whip.', 'Keldons were accustomed to rugged terrain, but they never expected it to be aggressive.', 'Legend has it the darba gave up its wings in return for an extra stomach.', 'Like a volcano, it too can erupt without warning.', 'Made strong by reckless magic. Made horrid by reckless strife.', 'Many travelers have wandered into a fog only to find that it had teeth, claws, and an appetite.', 'Mortal minds shrivel at its touch.', 'Most soldiers think of the sword as a weapon. In the hands of Zho monks, swords are also the strongest of shields.', 'Nothing could grow where the vile smoke had been, and no one could breathe it and live.', 'Our war is against suffering, not against those who cause it.\\n—Samite creed', 'Pity the tailor.', 'She seeks the warmth of the living.', 'Some lands are soothing, and their peace can be felt in the soul.', 'Sometimes everyone decides to go for help at the same time.', "The Keldons didn't know her name, but they still cursed her in battle.", "The Keldons took several of the steeds as trophies of war. They'd never seen such a light beast stand so firm.", 'The Keldons would never admit it, but Greel unsettles them, too.', 'The Kipamu League knew what Keld refused to acknowledge: the land could support no more.', 'The Vintara Forest welcomes its enemies with a crushing embrace.', 'The chattering forest fell silent as the otherworldly song began.', 'The circle buys time—an important commodity in battle.', 'The end of one life is merely the beginning of thousands more.', "The ground won't accept them.", 'The harder your strike, the stronger her defense.', 'The hunted can become the fiercest hunters.', 'The land is heavy with promise, the harvest ripe with betrayal.', 'The problem with mercenaries is that if you can buy their loyalty, others can too.', 'The problem with rebels is that they so quickly reject authority.', 'The scent of magic can rob you of your senses, blinding you to the world.', "There's no difference between bone and crystal when it's piercing your throat.", "There's no rest for a Keldon.", 'These nimble ships were designed for hit-and-run tactics.', 'They fight beyond thought, beyond fear, and beyond mercy.', 'They hide in dreams and whispers and faraway thoughts.', 'They turn geological upheaval into tactical advantage.', 'This plague chooses its victims.', 'Though a powerful constrictor, it prefers simply to drown its prey.', 'Though it moves like a living thing, anyone can tell it lacks a soul—not to mention mercy.', 'To outrace the griffin\\n—Kipamu expression meaning "to do the impossible"', 'Trained with the aid of rhystic magic, they become uneasy in its absence.', 'Trod on by a gargadon\\n—Kipamu expression meaning "wiped out"', 'Ultimately, it became a three-way battle: the land attacked both armies.', 'What wall can never be climbed, but is always scaled?\\n—Nakaya riddle', 'When eagles leave the sky, sailors leave the sea.', 'When the Lion roars, his cubs grow stronger.\\n—Kipamu saying', 'When you have given everything, then you are capable of anything.\\n—Well inscription', 'When you have given everything, then you have everything to gain.\\n—Well inscription', 'Wherever they went, the Keldons transformed the land into a weapon.', 'While armies battled across Jamuraa, beasts stalked the high places looking for victims.', "With each grunt of pain from Haddad, Greel's grin widened.", "Wound, maim, kill: it's all the same to a Keldon."]
artist: ['Aaron Boyd', 'Adam Rex', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alan Rabinowitz', 'Andrew Goldhawk', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Ben Thompson', 'Bradley Williams', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dana Knutson', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Dorman', 'David Martin', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Don Hazeltine', 'Donato Giancola', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Eric Peterson', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Hildebrandt & Tim Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Joel Biske', 'John Howe', 'John Matson', 'Kev Walker', 'Marc Fishman', 'Mark Brill', 'Mark Romanoski', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Ploog', 'Nelson DeCastro', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Ray Lago', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Rob Alexander', 'Roger Raupp', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas Gianni', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Val Mayerik', 'Wayne England', 'rk post']
